{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-166819",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To determine the amount of thinner the painter should use with $0.4$ liters of paint, we have to multiply $0.6$ by $0.4.$\n\nWe proceed by multiplying the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers.\n\nNotice that the second number has a leading $0$, which we ignore during the multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in $0.6$ and there is $1$ decimal place in $0.4.$\nTherefore, their product will have $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n\nSo, we take our value of $24$ and add a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\n\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{24}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nHence, $0.6\\times 0.4=0.24.$\n\nWe conclude that the painter should use $0.24$ liters of thinner in $0.4$ liters of paint.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
